WEBVTT

00:00.700 --> 00:07.360
There's a $2 trillion social welfare and
climate package is what it's being called.

00:08.460 --> 00:10.800
Well, part of that is going to be about
social welfare.

00:10.980 --> 00:12.660
Human infrastructure, as being termed.

00:12.820 --> 00:15.180
It might be paying people to stay home.

00:15.580 --> 00:20.240
Does that upset an already fragile labor
market right now

00:20.240 --> 00:24.200
where we have so many people not in the
labor force?

00:25.080 --> 00:29.660
Agriculture in particular, we really
struggle because we pay so much

00:29.660 --> 00:33.180
in that lower unskilled labor pool.

00:33.400 --> 00:36.380
And what if those people that are getting
20-plus-percent pay raises get

00:36.380 --> 00:38.580
another 20% in 2022?

00:39.380 --> 00:41.080
Or what if they don't even show up?

00:41.940 --> 00:45.320
That sign right there from July, I was on
my way to Wisconsin to do a speaking

00:45.320 --> 00:48.160
engagement. I pulled into Culver's. You
guys don't have Culver's out here. Maybe

00:48.160 --> 00:51.600
you do. I don't know. I pulled in to get
me a butter burger and to take a pee.

00:51.800 --> 00:53.040
What'd that sign say?

00:53.040 --> 00:56.520
Due to being short-staffed, our
dining room will be closed for the day.

00:56.560 --> 00:57.580
Drive-thru is open.

00:58.040 --> 01:01.100
You know how mad the Culver manager gets
when you pee in their drive-thru?

01:04.200 --> 01:04.700
Okay.

01:04.900 --> 01:09.200
[music]
